    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d101">

                <pb facs="0275" n="161" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg161"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.629/2</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the German Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Wiedfeldt</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-05-01"><hi rendition="#italic">May 1,
                        1924</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to refer to
                    suggested changes in the draft of the proposed convention to prevent the
                    smuggling of intoxicating liquors into the United States as set forth in a
                    communication from Doctor von Lewinski<anchor n="40" xml:id="d101-f1"/> to the
                    Solicitor for this Department under date of April 26, 1924.<anchor n="41"
                        xml:id="d101-f2"/> In accordance with <pb facs="0276" n="162" xml:id="pg162"
                    /> your suggestions, the following changes in the draft are acceptable to this
                    Government: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Preamble.</hi></p>
                        <p rendition="#flush">“… have appointed as their Plenipotentiaries: <list>
                                <item>The President of the United States of America, Mr. Charles
                                    Evans Hughes, Secretary of State of the United States of
                                    America,</item>
                                <item>The President of the German Empire, Dr. Otto Wiedfeldt, German
                                    Ambassador to the United States of America.”</item>
                            </list></p>
                        <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article II</hi>. (1)</p>
                        <p>“The President of the German Empire agrees that Germany will raise no
                            objection”.</p>
                        <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article VI, paragraph</hi>
                            2:</p>
                        <p>“The present Convention shall be duly ratified by the President of the
                            United States of America, by and with the advice and consent of the
                            Senate thereof, and by the President of the German Empire in accordance
                            with the requirements of the German Constitution”.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>I have the honor to attach hereto a text of the proposed draft incorporating the
                    changes above noted.<anchor n="42" xml:id="d101-f3"/></p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles E. Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d101-f1" n="40" xml:id="d101-f1-content">
                <p>Counselor of the German Embassy.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d101-f2" n="41" xml:id="d101-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; the suggested changes, all of which were accepted by the Department,
                    were indicated in the draft submitted with the German Ambassador’s note of Apr.
                    28, <hi rendition="#italic">supra.</hi></p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d101-f3" n="42" xml:id="d101-f3-content">
                <p>See signed convention, <hi rendition="#italic">infra.</hi></p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
